// NOTE: Benchmark generation, ambiguity blending, and label noise are implemented
// in C (internal/runtime/qadav_nn.c). This .ydv defines the benchmark spec & stub.
//
// QNMF Pillar 6: Ambiguous Mixed Complexity Task Benchmark (100 Tasks, 20% Ambiguous)
// Tier 0 (Easy, 30):      25 clear + 5 borderline (e.g., hard 3-digit arithmetic edge cases)
// Tier 1 (Medium, 30):    25 clear + 5 borderline (surface overlap across L0/L1/L2)
// Tier 2 (Hard, 20):      18 clear + 2 borderline (trap grid looking K=3-solvable needing K=5)
// Tier 3 (Very Hard, 20): 18 clear + 2 borderline (4-step logic looking 2-step on surface)
// Label Noise: --label_noise 0.04 (4% randomly flipped training/observed labels)

network TasksToySpec ⟦
    dense ⟬100⸴ 64⟭ ·
    relu ·
    dense ⟬64⸴ 4⟭ ·
⟧

process main⦅⦆ → int64 ⟦
    emit "TASKS_TOY_100_AMBIGUOUS_INITIALIZED" ·
    yield 0 ·
⟧
